{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Neural Network Bias.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Neural Network Bias.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"neural network bias neural network bias","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Neural Network Bias.md","fileName":"Neural Network Bias.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Neural Network Bias","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 00:13\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Artificial Neural Network Structure]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Artificial Neural Network Structure","Activation Function","Neural Network Weight","Decision Boundary","algorithms.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Neural Network Bias.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Neural Network Bias.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"neural network bias neural network bias","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Neural Network Bias.md","fileName":"Neural Network Bias.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Neural Network Bias","heading":"Neural Network Bias","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A neural-network bias is a numerical parameter added to an artificial neuron's weighted input before applying its [[Activation Function]]. It shifts the neuron's propensity to activate independently of the current input values.\n\nThe opposite of a bias can be interpreted as a threshold that the weighted sum must cross. Like a [[Neural Network Weight]], the bias is adjusted during training to reduce prediction loss.\n\nIn Kelleher's geometric example, changing the weight direction rotates a neuron's [[Decision Boundary]], while changing the bias translates that boundary away from the origin. A constant input fixed at one can treat the bias as another learned weight, allowing the same weighted-sum and matrix calculations to include it without a separate special-case update.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Artificial Neural Network Structure","Activation Function","Neural Network Weight","Decision Boundary","algorithms.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Neural Network Bias.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Neural Network Bias.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"neural network bias neural network bias","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Neural Network Bias.md","fileName":"Neural Network Bias.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Neural Network Bias","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algorithms.epub]]\n\n[[deeplearning_mit.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Artificial Neural Network Structure","Activation Function","Neural Network Weight","Decision Boundary","algorithms.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}